    "uncited": [
     "For detailed traversal, surface determination, and mesh coherence mechanisms, see [Surface extraction](29-surface-extraction.md).",
     "Only cells for which the mask value is true at all eight vertices contribute to the contour surface.",
     "It calls `Box2D::GetDrawElement` with the 2D map, dimensions, isovalue, and a boolean for smoothing to produce the output geometry.",
     "To minimize texture popping artifacts when using proxy geometry with clipping planes or pronounced concavities, double the number of key views.",
     "Isovalues that closely match the outermost surface specified by the transfer function produce the best results.",
     "A displacement of four degrees eliminates most popping artifacts for good surface proxies.",
     "Allows specification of a threshold value for geometry surface generation.",
     "Used only in Isosurface, Mesh, Ocean Mesh, and Cap Mesh Modes.",
     "For Phoenix liquids (range 0-1, where 0 is no liquid and 1 is 100% full), an Isosurface Level of 0.5 is best for visualizing the surface between air and liquid.",
     "For imported caches from Houdini (positive/negative values indicating inside/outside), the correct 'halfway' Isosurface Level value is 0.0.",
     "For Phoenix smoke, the proper Isosurface Level value is about 0.01."
    ]
